# Documentation map

Each artifact answers exactly one question. If two documents would say the same thing, one of them
links to the other instead.

| Question | Artifact |
|---|---|
| Why are we building this, and for whom? | [PRD.md](../PRD.md) |
| How will it be built? | [TRD.md](../TRD.md) |
| What did we decide, and why? | [adr/](adr/) |
| What is the architecture context? | [architecture/](architecture/) |
| What does it look like? | [WIREFRAME.md](../WIREFRAME.md) |
| What are the visual rules? | [DESIGN.md](../DESIGN.md) |
| How do I contribute? | [CONTRIBUTING.md](../CONTRIBUTING.md) |
| What must an agent know? | [AGENTS.md](../AGENTS.md) |

## The architecture repository

`docs/architecture/` **is** this project's Architecture Repository in TOGAF terms. The ADM is used as
a reference model, not a process model — it does not mandate phase sequence, a waterfall process, or
any phase duration. The ten phases collapse into three verbs here:

| Verb | ADM phases | What it produces in this repo |
|---|---|---|
| **Understand** | A–D | [vision.md](architecture/vision.md), and TRD sections 5–7 |
| **Specify** | E–F | [roadmap.md](architecture/roadmap.md), TRD section 11 |
| **Govern** | G–H | [adr/](adr/), CI gates, CODEOWNERS |

Requirements Management runs continuously and lives in the PRD register plus the TRD traceability
matrix. Enterprise-level deliverables — organizational model, communications plan, capability
assessment, formal architecture contracts — are deliberately out of scope for a single code
repository.

## Traceability

Five ID families, assigned once and never renumbered: `FR-`/`NFR-` (PRD), `US` (stories), `SCR-`
(screens), `ADR-` (decisions), `T` (tasks). The single matrix lives in TRD section 4 and is validated
in CI by `scripts/check-docs`.

## Unresolved points

Anywhere in the spine, tag something still undecided by prefixing the line with the clarification
marker — the literal text `[NEEDS` `CLARIFICATION:` joined together, followed by the question and a
closing bracket. `scripts/check-docs` counts them and fails the build while any remain, so an
unresolved specification cannot reach `{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}`.

Use it liberally during drafting. It is a gate, not a criticism.
